.TH START-MU2EDAQ-RUNLOG-DB.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-runlog-db t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start-mu2edaq-runlog-db.sh \- control-room start wrapper for the run-log viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start\-mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.sh
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standardised Mu2e control-room start script, run by
.B crs-app start runlog-db
(entry
.B runlog\-db
in
.IR mu2edaq\-controlroom\-setup/config/apps.yaml ,
.BR "ports: {http: 8000}" ).
It sets
.B RUNLOGDB_PORT
and
.BR exec s
.BR start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1)
with any arguments, which that script ignores.
.PP
This file and
.B start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer
are both regular files in git (mode 100755), not symbolic links; this one is
a two-line adapter, not a duplicate.
.PP
The wrapper does not set
.BR DJANGO_ENV ,
and nothing in mu2edaq-main does, so a control-room launch runs in
development mode: no authentication, every request is the superuser
.BR dev ,
DEBUG on, and a local SQLite database rather than the production run log.
See
.BR start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1).
.SH OPTIONS
None of its own.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_HTTP
Port exported by the control-room launcher.
Takes precedence over
.BR RUNLOGDB_PORT .
.TP
.B RUNLOGDB_PORT
Used when
.B CRS_PORT_HTTP
is unset; default 8000.
.SH EXIT STATUS
That of
.BR start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
CRS_PORT_HTTP=8000 ./start\-mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.sh
DJANGO_ENV=production ./start\-mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.sh
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.sh (1),
.BR start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
